# Firehorse Skillful Report — Annual Sustainability Report

**Report type:** Annual Sustainability Report (CSRD/ESRS compliant)
**Agent:** `src/firehorse/report-module.ts` (format: `annual-report`)
**CLI:** `dws firehorse-report --format annual-report --input '{"organizationId":"org-1","industry":"steel","periodStart":"2025-01-01","periodEnd":"2025-12-31"}'`
**API:** `POST /api/v1/firehorse/reports/generate` with `{"format":"annual-report","organizationId":"...","industry":"...","periodStart":"...","periodEnd":"..."}`
**Validation:** 4-week validation workflow before signing

## What This Skill Knows

Full CSRD Annual Report generation aligned to EFRAG ESRS 2023 final standards. Replaces 200+ hours of manual consultant-driven reporting with one automated template fed by DWS IQ compliance agent data.

## Report Architecture (ESRS Structure)

### ESRS 2 — General Disclosures

- Governance: board oversight, sustainability governance structure
- Strategy: business model, value chain, stakeholder engagement
- Material impacts, risks and opportunities (double materiality)
- Metrics and targets

### ESRS E1 — Climate Change

- GHG emissions (Scope 1, 2, 3) — source: ETS/CBAM agent data
- Energy consumption and mix
- Physical and transition climate risks
- Climate targets aligned to Paris Agreement / Science Based Targets

### ESRS E2–E5 (if material)

- E2: Pollution
- E3: Water and marine resources
- E4: Biodiversity and ecosystems
- E5: Resource use and circular economy

### ESRS S1 — Own Workforce

- Worker health and safety (EN 13001, ISO 45001 — SiteSense agent data)
- Working conditions, remuneration, diversity

### ESRS G1 — Business Conduct

- Business ethics, anti-corruption
- Political engagement
- Supplier relationships and payment practices

## 82 ESRS Data Points Coverage

Full registry at `src/compliance/esrs-registry.ts`. Report flags:

- ✅ Data available (from ERP, IoT, agent data)
- ⚠️ Estimated (methodology documented)
- ❌ Not yet collected (gap action required)

## Validation Workflow

```
Week 1: Data ingestion (ERP sync + compliance agent scoring)
Week 2: Draft report generation + internal review
Week 3: External auditor data package preparation
Week 4: Final sign-off + DocuSign attestation
```

## Output Format

```json
{
  "format": "annual-report",
  "year": 2025,
  "esrsCoverage": { "total": 82, "available": number, "estimated": number, "gaps": number },
  "scope1": number,
  "scope2": number,
  "scope3": number,
  "euTaxonomyAlignment": number,
  "markdown": "full annual report as markdown",
  "auditorPackage": "data export for external verification",
  "signed": boolean
}
```

## Standards References

- EFRAG ESRS 2023 final set — 82 disclosure requirements
- EU Directive 2022/2464 (CSRD) — mandatory for large companies >500 employees or >€50M turnover
- GRI Universal Standards 2021 — aligned interoperability
- EU Taxonomy Regulation 2020/852 — sustainable activity classification
- TCFD — Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures
